Upgrade instructions:

The DAV database gets upgraded automatically, but two kinds of existing data
predate this change and need attention:

Existing JMAP calendar event notifications do not record the privacy of the
event they are about, so they keep being visible to sharees. Purge them from
the JMAP notification folder to make CLASS take effect for them.

Existing DAV database entries may hold a stale privacy. A sharee still can
read such an event, although they may not write it. Run "dav_reconstruct" to
refresh these entries.


